{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-30527","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33824","text":"webhost.systems — [&] Protocol Integration Spec (v1)"}]},{"id":"blk-30528","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33825","text":"Version: 1.0 Status: Draft Audience: Engineering Last updated: 2026-03-28"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30530","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33826","text":"This document extends the v1 spec to make WebHost.Systems the canonical hosting layer for [&] Protocol agents."}]}],"id":"blk-30529","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-30531","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33827","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-30532","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33828","text":"0) Context"}]},{"id":"blk-30533","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33829","text":"WebHost.Systems currently treats agents as opaque code bundles deployed to Cloudflare Workers or AWS AgentCore. To serve as the hosting platform for the [&] Protocol ecosystem, WHS must understand "},{"id":"spn-33830","marks":["bold"],"text":"capability declarations"},{"id":"spn-33831","text":", "},{"id":"spn-33832","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP sidecar orchestration"},{"id":"spn-33833","text":", "},{"id":"spn-33834","marks":["bold"],"text":"agent-to-agent skill routing"},{"id":"spn-33835","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-33836","marks":["bold"],"text":"governance enforcement"},{"id":"spn-33837","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-30534","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33838","text":"This spec adds [&]-aware features as phased extensions to the existing v1 architecture. The current CRUD/deploy/invoke/telemetry foundation remains intact."}]},{"id":"blk-30535","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33839","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-30536","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33840","text":"1) Capability Manifests (ampersand.json)"}]},{"id":"blk-30537","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33841","text":"1.1 Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-30538","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33842","text":"Agents currently declare only "},{"id":"spn-33843","marks":["code"],"text":"name"},{"id":"spn-33844","text":", "},{"id":"spn-33845","marks":["code"],"text":"description"},{"id":"spn-33846","text":", "},{"id":"spn-33847","marks":["code"],"text":"framework"},{"id":"spn-33848","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-33849","marks":["code"],"text":"runtimeProvider"},{"id":"spn-33850","text":". There is no way for the platform to know what capabilities an agent uses ("},{"id":"spn-33851","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-33852","text":", "},{"id":"spn-33853","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-33854","text":", etc.) or what it provides."}]},{"id":"blk-30539","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33855","text":"1.2 Solution"}]},{"id":"blk-30540","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33856","text":"Support an optional "},{"id":"spn-33857","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-33858","text":" manifest alongside the agent code bundle. When present, WHS validates it against the [&] Protocol schema and uses it for:"}]},{"id":"blk-30541","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30543","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33859","text":"Capability-aware deployment (auto-provision required MCP sidecars)"}]}],"id":"blk-30542","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30545","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33860","text":"FleetPrompt registry integration (publish agent capabilities)"}]}],"id":"blk-30544","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30547","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33861","text":"Governance enforcement (Delegatic policy checks)"}]}],"id":"blk-30546","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30548","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33862","text":"1.3 Schema"}]},{"id":"blk-30549","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33863","text":"The manifest follows "},{"id":"spn-33864","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/protocol/schema/v0.1.0/ampersand.schema.json"},{"id":"spn-33865","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-30550","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33866","text":"Key fields for WHS:"}]},{"id":"blk-30551","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"agent\": \"my-agent\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"uses\": [\"&memory.graph\", \"&time.anomaly\", \"&reason.deliberate\"],\n    \"provides\": [\"&space.fleet.locate\"]\n  },\n  \"providers\": {\n    \"&memory.graph\": { \"provider\": \"graphonomous\", \"config\": { \"db\": \"auto\" } },\n    \"&time.anomaly\": { \"provider\": \"ticktickclock\" },\n    \"&reason.deliberate\": { \"provider\": \"auto\" }\n  },\n  \"governance\": {\n    \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n    \"constraints\": { \"hard\": [\"no_network_without_approval\"], \"soft\": [] }\n  },\n  \"mcp_servers\": [\"graphonomous\", \"ticktickclock\"]\n}"},{"id":"blk-30552","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33867","text":"1.4 Data Model Extension"}]},{"id":"blk-30553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33868","text":"Add to "},{"id":"spn-33869","marks":["code"],"text":"agents"},{"id":"spn-33870","text":" table:"}]},{"id":"blk-30554","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"ampersandManifest: optional JSON blob (validated against schema on deploy)\ncapabilitiesUsed: optional string[] (denormalized from manifest for search/filter)\ncapabilitiesProvided: optional string[] (denormalized for registry)"},{"id":"blk-30555","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33871","text":"1.5 Validation"}]},{"id":"blk-30556","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33872","text":"On deployment, if "},{"id":"spn-33873","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-33874","text":" is present in the bundle: 1. Validate against [&] schema (reuse "},{"id":"spn-33875","marks":["code"],"text":"@ampersand-protocol/validate"},{"id":"spn-33876","text":" npm package) 2. Extract "},{"id":"spn-33877","marks":["code"],"text":"capabilities.uses"},{"id":"spn-33878","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-33879","marks":["code"],"text":"capabilities.provides"},{"id":"spn-33880","text":" 3. Verify all declared providers are available in the deployment environment 4. Store validated manifest in "},{"id":"spn-33881","marks":["code"],"text":"agents.ampersandManifest"}]},{"id":"blk-30557","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33882","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-30558","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33883","text":"2) MCP Sidecar Orchestration"}]},{"id":"blk-30559","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33884","text":"2.1 Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-30560","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33885","text":"[&] agents compose capabilities via MCP servers (Graphonomous for "},{"id":"spn-33886","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-33887","text":", TickTickClock for "},{"id":"spn-33888","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-33889","text":", etc.). Currently WHS deploys agents in isolation with no MCP server connectivity."}]},{"id":"blk-30561","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33890","text":"2.2 Solution"}]},{"id":"blk-30562","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33891","marks":["bold"],"text":"Phase 1 — Linked MCP services"},{"id":"spn-33892","text":": Allow agents to declare MCP server dependencies. WHS provisions and manages these as linked services (similar to linked databases in PaaS platforms)."}]},{"id":"blk-30563","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33893","marks":["bold"],"text":"Phase 2 — MCP sidecar model"},{"id":"spn-33894","text":": For Cloudflare Workers, run MCP servers as Durable Object sidecars. For AgentCore, use linked Lambda/container sidecars."}]},{"id":"blk-30564","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33895","text":"2.3 Configuration"}]},{"id":"blk-30565","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33896","text":"In "},{"id":"spn-33897","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-33898","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-30566","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"mcp_servers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"graphonomous\",\n      \"transport\": \"streamable_http\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"db_path\": \"auto\",\n        \"embedder_backend\": \"fallback\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-30567","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33899","text":"2.4 Data Model Extension"}]},{"id":"blk-30568","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33900","text":"New table: "},{"id":"spn-33901","marks":["code"],"text":"linkedServices"}]},{"id":"blk-30569","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"agentId: Id<\"agents\">\nserviceType: \"mcp_server\" | \"database\" | \"cache\"\nserviceName: string\nproviderRef: string (provider-specific endpoint/identifier)\nconfig: JSON\nstatus: \"provisioning\" | \"active\" | \"error\" | \"deprovisioned\"\ncreatedAt: number"},{"id":"blk-30570","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33902","text":"2.5 Runtime Provider Interface Extension"}]},{"id":"blk-30571","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33903","text":"Add to RPI (§20):"}]},{"id":"blk-30572","kind":"code","language":"typescript","text":"interface RuntimeProviderAdapter {\n  // ... existing methods ...\n\n  // Phase 2: MCP sidecar support\n  provisionLinkedService?(agentId: string, service: LinkedServiceConfig): Promise<ServiceRef>;\n  deprovisionLinkedService?(agentId: string, serviceRef: string): Promise<void>;\n  getLinkedServiceEndpoint?(agentId: string, serviceName: string): Promise<string>;\n}"},{"id":"blk-30573","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33904","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-30574","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33905","text":"3) Agent-to-Agent Skill Routing (A2A)"}]},{"id":"blk-30575","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33906","text":"3.1 Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-30576","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33907","text":"Currently only human→agent invocation is supported. [&] agents need to invoke skills on other agents (e.g., a fleet coordinator querying a spatial intelligence agent)."}]},{"id":"blk-30577","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33908","text":"3.2 Solution"}]},{"id":"blk-30578","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33909","text":"Add A2A invocation support using the A2A protocol (agent-to-agent, complementary to MCP):"}]},{"id":"blk-30579","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33910","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-33911","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skill declaration"},{"id":"spn-33912","text":": Agents declare "},{"id":"spn-33913","marks":["code"],"text":"a2a_skills"},{"id":"spn-33914","text":" in their manifest 2. "},{"id":"spn-33915","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skill discovery"},{"id":"spn-33916","text":": WHS maintains an internal skill registry (derived from manifests) 3. "},{"id":"spn-33917","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skill invocation"},{"id":"spn-33918","text":": Agents can invoke skills on other agents via a WHS-mediated endpoint 4. "},{"id":"spn-33919","marks":["bold"],"text":"Governance"},{"id":"spn-33920","text":": All A2A calls pass through Delegatic policy checks"}]},{"id":"blk-30580","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33921","text":"3.3 API Extension"}]},{"id":"blk-30581","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"POST /api/v1/a2a/invoke\n{\n  \"caller_agent_id\": \"agent_abc\",\n  \"skill\": \"fleet-state-enrichment\",\n  \"input\": { ... },\n  \"session_id\": \"optional\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-30582","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33922","text":"WHS resolves the skill to a target agent, checks governance policies, invokes the target, and returns the result."}]},{"id":"blk-30583","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33923","text":"3.4 Data Model Extension"}]},{"id":"blk-30584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33924","text":"New table: "},{"id":"spn-33925","marks":["code"],"text":"skillRegistry"}]},{"id":"blk-30585","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"agentId: Id<\"agents\">\nskill: string\ncapability: string (&space.fleet, etc.)\nstatus: \"active\" | \"inactive\""},{"id":"blk-30586","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33926","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-30587","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33927","text":"4) Governance Enforcement (Delegatic Integration)"}]},{"id":"blk-30588","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33928","text":"4.1 Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-30589","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33929","text":"WHS currently enforces only tier-based billing limits. [&] agents need governance enforcement: hard/soft constraints, autonomy levels, goal-aware authorization, and audit trails."}]},{"id":"blk-30590","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33930","text":"4.2 Solution"}]},{"id":"blk-30591","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33931","text":"Integrate with Delegatic for governance:"}]},{"id":"blk-30592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33932","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-33933","marks":["bold"],"text":"Policy attachment"},{"id":"spn-33934","text":": Link agents to Delegatic org/policy trees 2. "},{"id":"spn-33935","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pre-invocation check"},{"id":"spn-33936","text":": Before invoking an agent, check Delegatic policies 3. "},{"id":"spn-33937","marks":["bold"],"text":"Audit forwarding"},{"id":"spn-33938","text":": Forward invocation telemetry to Delegatic audit trail 4. "},{"id":"spn-33939","marks":["bold"],"text":"Autonomy enforcement"},{"id":"spn-33940","text":": Respect "},{"id":"spn-33941","marks":["code"],"text":"observe | advise | act"},{"id":"spn-33942","text":" autonomy levels from manifests"}]},{"id":"blk-30593","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33943","text":"4.3 Configuration"}]},{"id":"blk-30594","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33944","text":"In "},{"id":"spn-33945","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-33946","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-30595","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"governance\": {\n    \"delegatic_org_id\": \"org_xyz\",\n    \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n    \"constraints\": {\n      \"hard\": [\"no_network_without_approval\", \"no_filesystem_write\"],\n      \"soft\": [\"prefer_local_inference\"]\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-30596","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33947","text":"4.4 Invocation Flow Change"}]},{"id":"blk-30597","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33948","text":"Updated Flow C (Invoke agent): 1. Client calls "},{"id":"spn-33949","marks":["code"],"text":"POST /invoke/:agentId"},{"id":"spn-33950","text":" 2. Control plane authenticates/authorizes 3. "},{"id":"spn-33951","marks":["bold"],"text":"NEW"},{"id":"spn-33952","text":": If agent has governance config, call Delegatic policy check 4. Check plan limits and agent status 5. Route to runtime provider 6. "},{"id":"spn-33953","marks":["bold"],"text":"NEW"},{"id":"spn-33954","text":": Forward telemetry to Delegatic audit 7. Return response"}]},{"id":"blk-30598","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33955","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-30599","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33956","text":"5) Provider Registry (Dynamic Resolution)"}]},{"id":"blk-30600","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33957","text":"5.1 Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-30601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33958","text":"Runtime providers (Cloudflare, AgentCore) are hardcoded. [&] agents declare capability providers that should be resolved dynamically (e.g., "},{"id":"spn-33959","marks":["code"],"text":"\"provider\": \"auto\""},{"id":"spn-33960","text":" should resolve to the best available provider for "},{"id":"spn-33961","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-33962","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-30602","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33963","text":"5.2 Solution"}]},{"id":"blk-30603","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33964","text":"Add a capability provider registry to WHS:"}]},{"id":"blk-30604","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Provider: graphonomous → Capabilities: [&memory.graph, &memory.consolidate, &reason.deliberate, &reason.attend]\nProvider: ticktickclock → Capabilities: [&time.anomaly, &time.forecast, &time.pattern]\nProvider: geofleetic → Capabilities: [&space.fleet, &space.route, &space.geofence]\nProvider: bendscript → Capabilities: [&memory.graph (KAG)]"},{"id":"blk-30605","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33965","text":"When "},{"id":"spn-33966","marks":["code"],"text":"\"provider\": \"auto\""},{"id":"spn-33967","text":", WHS resolves to the best available provider based on: 1. Capability match 2. Provider availability in deployment region 3. Cost tier of the user's plan 4. Governance constraints"}]},{"id":"blk-30606","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33968","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-30607","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33969","text":"6) Provenance and Audit Trail"}]},{"id":"blk-30608","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33970","text":"6.1 Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-30609","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33971","text":"Currently invocations have basic "},{"id":"spn-33972","marks":["code"],"text":"traceId"},{"id":"spn-33973","text":" but no hash-linked provenance chain. For [&] agents, every decision should be traceable back through the capability calls that informed it."}]},{"id":"blk-30610","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33974","text":"6.2 Solution"}]},{"id":"blk-30611","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33975","text":"Extend telemetry events with provenance fields:"}]},{"id":"blk-30612","kind":"code","language":"typescript","text":"interface TelemetryEvent {\n  // ... existing fields ...\n\n  // [&] provenance extension\n  ampersand?: {\n    capabilities_invoked: string[];      // [\"&memory.graph.recall\", \"&time.anomaly.detect\"]\n    routing_decision: \"fast\" | \"deliberate\";  // κ routing result\n    kappa_value?: number;                // cyclicity score if deliberation was triggered\n    goal_id?: string;                    // Graphonomous GoalGraph reference\n    provenance_hash?: string;            // hash-linked to parent invocation\n    a2a_calls?: {\n      target_agent: string;\n      skill: string;\n      duration_ms: number;\n    }[];\n  };\n}"},{"id":"blk-30613","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33976","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-30614","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33977","text":"7) Implementation Phases"}]},{"id":"blk-30615","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33978","text":"Phase 1 — Manifest Support (lowest lift, highest signal)"}]},{"id":"blk-30616","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30618","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33979","text":"[ ] Accept "},{"id":"spn-33980","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-33981","text":" in deployment bundles"}]}],"id":"blk-30617","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33982","text":"[ ] Validate against [&] schema using "},{"id":"spn-33983","marks":["code"],"text":"@ampersand-protocol/validate"}]}],"id":"blk-30619","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30622","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33984","text":"[ ] Store manifest + denormalized capabilities in "},{"id":"spn-33985","marks":["code"],"text":"agents"},{"id":"spn-33986","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-30621","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30624","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33987","text":"[ ] Add capability filter to agent list API"}]}],"id":"blk-30623","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30626","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33988","text":"[ ] Update dashboard to show declared capabilities"}]}],"id":"blk-30625","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30627","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-33989","text":"Phase 2 — MCP Linked Services"}]},{"id":"blk-30628","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30630","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33990","text":"[ ] Design linked service provisioning for Cloudflare (Durable Object sidecars)"}]}],"id":"blk-30629","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30632","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-33991","text":"[ ] Design linked service provi